:answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403669}] :question/id #uuid "701f0d82-dd3a-58b3-b64b-6042ce1e752a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73612" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $2$nd and $4$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d3d7552-73fd-5a30-adca-213fce95daf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410765} {:answer/id #uuid "2c231bf1-1c62-5bb0-a5af-80fd235dc05d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410766} {:answer/id #uuid "88eecdfd-f245-5138-93d4-a347d38063c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410767} {:answer/id #uuid "a582f1d6-9082-5ca9-8a15-8892198e09a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410768} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2f5437-3869-5765-88a5-9a58e75de19b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410765} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec2a6fc-f001-5e94-83d4-c400fba8593b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410770}] :question/id #uuid "bcd1cb26-1c44-5d74-aa8e-2093ab435f98" :question/math-academy-id "q-130950" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c750eaf-692f-5572-bdcf-255079d52728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414468} {:answer/id #uuid "439cc40e-3b18-56fc-b431-aca3fb7a238d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414469} {:answer/id #uuid "82e06dac-e13b-51bb-b072-e0b02f1d17f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414475} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaf59cb-72f9-5884-b2ae-369f981d4b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414482} {:answer/id #uuid "cf412197-e968-5ab2-9ca2-3bedc14b3ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414475} :answer-field/id #uuid "846e9557-c707-56d2-86ec-10035a40ea93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414492}] :question/id #uuid "ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73613" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b45315b-a5c2-53a7-b6d0-069454aca98b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565696} {:answer/id #uuid "384525a8-6bc7-511c-89ba-ed88a8ddda66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565770} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed2e27a-0bf7-5dd2-b5c6-be0e98115df1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565803} {:answer/id #uuid "68cc9e55-2409-512a-ac2e-c70b873bffd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565841} {:answer/id #uuid "e0608257-5e3b-5666-af66-4b0ccd77c69a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565770} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e5f4d81-f91b-55ef-9252-1ab82323e853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566167}] :question/id #uuid "75f69126-c110-5545-9efd-4ceeba235a0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73615" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Non-Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124292 :question/id #uuid "6e4b2e85-86a8-5050-a60a-ae8d40453ad0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4705" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](images/df/dfe650778e528254fc2098714566d954c47442ede485d6a92495cf16eb9e936d.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561101 :question-generator/id #uuid "1a826b59-74a9-5e36-9c52-67364fe51a6d" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124479.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bf2fc69-40c7-50ed-b76f-0a01f02146c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414464} {:answer/id #uuid "442b7450-7d3f-5b57-8244-47e2ea21ed79" :answ