rix by permuting its columns. Therefore, $A$ is a permutation matrix.\n\nThe inverse of a permutation matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}={P}^{T}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b44952f5-62c3-54e0-971a-c074a603e5e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388350} {:answer/id #uuid "76a55830-f573-557a-86b4-f7fd6c91b784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388351} {:answer/id #uuid "75c59d61-cce9-5c55-9a48-18a878b74fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388352} {:answer/id #uuid "1396f24a-f1a9-5cce-a6d9-1e5353ea4dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388353} {:answer/id #uuid "9db32bd0-c3fb-56b8-bf6e-15f86755369c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388354} :answer-field/id #uuid "27c5440f-07dc-5142-bcfe-40c7293a7902" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388349}] :question/id #uuid "40f40cda-7847-5c65-80b1-4137ece3b7f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-135366" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix can be obtained from the identity matrix by permuting its columns. Therefore, $A$ is a permutation matrix.\n\nThe inverse of a permutation matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}={P}^{T}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c586833d-f519-5db2-986f-97a6e2667402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388357} {:answer/id #uuid "ee43d0e8-4c86-502d-abfd-84b12cc35959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388358} {:answer/id #uuid "2271aec9-a2b4-5a0a-a941-63ed32717332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388359} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebb0741-3775-5ad3-9a33-06de8b3bb023" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388360} {:answer/id #uuid "14150974-642c-58c2-9a04-41aa467ace14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388358} :answer-field/id #uuid "d12a4dde-d3e7-5f26-82ea-8ff8d75d25e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388356}] :question/id #uuid "ab7ab5ac-cf9c-5408-a789-f3b32435589c" :question/math-academy-id "q-135373" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix can be obtained from the identity matrix by permuting its columns. Therefore, $A$ is a permutation matrix.\n\nThe inverse of a permutation matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}={P}^{T}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Permutation Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054698 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054594 :question/id #uuid "dc76800e-9705-51b0-8b0d-027b85cf45b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-8936" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n![](images/66/66e85832b6e97aaf425f7cfe62c900cf0d476a4d3418405d6b029d7c04dbbff8.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we're given a Frobenius matrix:\n\n- all entries on the main diagonal are ones\n\n- the matrix has only one column (the $1$st column) where some entries below the main diagonal are not zeros\n\n- all the other entries outside the main diagonal are zeros\n\nTo find the inverse of a Frobenius matrix, we simply change the signs of the non-zero entries outside the main diagonal.\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={